  "howToReadTheHeader": "The source’s own header reads \"status: failed / reason: WRITE_FAILED\". That is the capture flow failing to WRITE its output to its intended destination, not a failure of the retrieval: found_count is 20 of 26 requested, every one of the 20 carries a full raw_flow_resource, and the 6 misses are recorded individually with the API error that produced them. The header was read as \"the data is bad\" once in this work and the whole write surface was left unexamined for it.",
