  "whatThisEstablishes": [
    "Twenty of twenty flows read live in this tenant on 2026-09-18 carried triggerAuthenticationType = All. Not one carried Tenant. See laterReadings: one of them, IP_SCAN_INTAKE, was restored to Tenant on 2026-09-24.",
    "All twenty are in state Started, so none of this is a description of something switched off.",
    "The 32-hex applicationWorkflowId ↔ dashed powerAutomateFlowId join, for 20 of the 25 wired contract keys. That join is what GOV-06 records as missing: export packages carry full_resource_id: null, so nothing in a package resolves to the workflow id in a trigger URL. This reading resolves it from the tenant side instead."
  ],
  "whatItExplicitlyDoesNotEstablish": [
    "Which of two candidate flows serves an endpoint, where the registry offers two. See joinIsOneToManyForSomeWorkflows.",
    "That the estate is 20 flows. It is the 20 that this capture asked for and found; 6 more were requested and not returned, and the repository wires 25 contract keys behind 23 physical flows.",
    "That no flow anywhere carries Tenant. It establishes that none of these twenty does.",
    "Anything about the endpoint URLs. The registry records below carry endpointStatus TENANT_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED, which is the capture declining to assert that the URL it mapped is the one in use. That reservation is about the URL mapping; the definition read beside it is a direct API read and carries no such reservation."
  ],
